(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #103 and #108: a global text that owns a string it
 built frees that string when it is set again, unless something else may
 still hold it. A field written from the text is such a holder, so the
 text stops freeing; and a text read FROM a field never frees the field's
 string, only the strings it built itself. Fifty reassignments each way,
 and the field still reads what it was given.)

A thing called note has
  a text called body is "".

a number called seed is 7.
a text called owned is "built {seed}".
a note called kept.
Set kept's body to owned.
Repeat 50 times,
  Set owned to "{owned}+".
Print kept.

a text called reader is "first {seed}".
Set reader to kept's body.
Repeat 50 times,
  Set reader to "{reader}-".
Print kept.
Print reader.
